        "summary":  "The article identifies six critical decision tensions facing CIOs: foundational IT investment versus growth initiatives, innovation versus operational resilience, innovation versus risk management, speed versus organizational readiness, data accessibility versus data protection, and AI cost versus AI benefit. The piece argues that AI has sharpened all six tensions simultaneously while raising expectations from boards, business units, and regulators. The author frames these not as problems to solve once but as ongoing balancing acts requiring structured governance.",
