        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Author Saurabh Joshi argues that embedding compliance into technology architecture from inception ΓÇö rather than bolting it on retroactively ΓÇö creates measurable competitive differentiation. Three strategies are proposed: controls-by-design architectural patterns, cross-functional accountability alignment, and leveraging specialized compliance partnerships. Payments industry examples illustrate how regulatory readiness translates into faster product launches, stronger customer trust, and reduced remediation costs.",
